        "content": "# Design Decisions: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Created**: 2026-01-30\n\n## Decision Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML parsing library | js-yaml v4.1.0 | User-approved dependency; provides YAMLException with mark.line and mark.column for precise error location; YAML 1.1/1.2 compatible; pure JavaScript works with Bun | None viable after constraint relaxation |\n| D2 | Module structure | Separate yaml-validator.ts from validate.ts CLI | Enables unit testing of core logic without CLI; follows single responsibility principle; matches existing project pattern (utils.ts) | Single file approach (reduced testability) |\n| D3 | Exit code scheme | 0=success, 1=syntax error, 2=file error | Unix convention; distinguishes validation failures from file access errors; enables fine-grained CI/CD handling | Single non-zero code for all errors |\n| D4 | File I/O approach | Bun.file().text() async | Native Bun API; non-blocking; consistent with modern async/await patterns | Node.js fs module (less Bun-idiomatic); sync read (blocking) |\n| D5 | Extension handling | Accept any extension | Requirements say .yaml/.yml \"are processed\" but do not mandate restriction; more flexible for edge cases | Reject non-.yaml/.yml files (overly restrictive interpretation) |\n| D6 | ValidationResult interface | Return object with success, error, line, column | Structured data enables flexible CLI formatting; supports future JSON output if needed; explicit over boolean return | Simple boolean return (loses error details); throw exceptions (control flow misuse) |\n| D7 | Error message format | Human-readable with file, line, column | Matches REQ-005 for line numbers; consistent format aids user experience; includes enough context without overwhelming | Raw js-yaml error (too technical); minimal output (insufficient detail) |\n| D8 | Test approach | Unit test validateYamlContent, integration test validateYamlFile | validateYamlContent testable without file fixtures; validateYamlFile validates integration; avoids testing js-yaml internals | E2E only (slow); mock js-yaml (tests mocks not code) |\n\n## AFK Mode: Auto-Selected Technology Decisions\n\n| Decision | Choice | Source | Rationale |\n|----------|--------|--------|-----------|\n| YAML library | js-yaml | User clarification | Explicitly permitted by user; well-established library |\n| Runtime | Bun | Codebase pattern | package.json shows bun test, bun run scripts |\n| Language | TypeScript | Codebase pattern | All source files are .ts |\n| Test framework | bun:test | Codebase pattern | Existing utils.test.ts uses bun:test |\n| File structure | src/ directory | Codebase pattern | Existing code in src/index.ts, src/utils.ts |\n| Test file location | Co-located *.test.ts | Codebase pattern | Existing src/utils.test.ts pattern |\n| Module system | ES modules | Codebase pattern | package.json \"type\": \"module\" |\n"
