        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 5 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 days\n**Started**: 2026-01-30\n\n## Overview\n\nA command-line YAML syntax validator that reads a YAML file from the local filesystem, parses it using the js-yaml library, and reports success or failure with actionable error messages including line numbers. The validator is invoked via `bun run validate <filepath>` and returns appropriate exit codes for CI/CD integration.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation: add js-yaml dependency\n2. [T2] - Core module implementation (requires js-yaml)\n3. [T3, T4] - CLI and tests can be developed in parallel (both use validator)\n4. [T5] - Script registration (requires CLI to exist)\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (imports js-yaml library)\n- T3 -> T2 (imports validateYamlFile function)\n- T4 -> T2 (tests validateYamlContent function)\n- T5 -> T3 (script must point to existing entry point)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T3 -> T5\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Add js-yaml dependency to package.json `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#4-technology-stack](design.md#4-technology-stack)\n\n    **Effort**: 1 hour\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] js-yaml ^4.1.0 added to dependencies in package.json\n    - [ ] `bun install` completes successfully\n    - [ ] js-yaml can be imported in TypeScript files\n\n### Core Module\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement yaml-validator.ts with ValidationResult interface and validation functions `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-module-yaml-validatorts](design.md#31-module-yaml-validatorts)\n\n    **Effort**: 5 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] ValidationResult interface exported with success, filepath, error, line, and column properties\n    - [ ] validateYamlFile async function reads file using Bun.file API and returns ValidationResult\n    - [ ] validateYamlContent sync function validates YAML string and returns ValidationResult\n    - [ ] Valid YAML content returns {success: true, filepath}\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML returns {success: false, error, line, column} extracted from YAMLException\n    - [ ] Non-existent file returns {success: false, error: \"File not found\"}\n    - [ ] Empty content treated as valid YAML\n\n### CLI and Tests\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement validate.ts CLI entry point with argument parsing and formatted output `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-module-validatets](design.md#32-module-validatets)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] CLI accepts single filepath argument from process.argv\n    - [ ] Missing argument displays usage message and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] Valid YAML displays \"Valid YAML: {filepath}\" and exits with code 0\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML displays \"Invalid YAML: {filepath}\" with error details including line/column and exits with code 1\n    - [ ] File not found displays \"Error: File not found: {filepath}\" and exits with code 2\n    - [ ] Output format matches design specification\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Implement unit tests for yaml-validator.ts `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Test file created at src/yaml-validator.test.ts\n    - [ ] Test: validateYamlContent returns success for valid YAML\n    - [ ] Test: validateYamlContent returns success for empty content\n    - [ ] Test: validateYamlContent returns error with line number for invalid YAML\n    - [ ] Test: validateYamlContent returns error with column number for invalid YAML\n    - [ ] Test: validateYamlContent handles YAML with comments\n    - [ ] Test: validateYamlContent handles multi-document YAML\n    - [ ] Test: validateYamlFile returns success for valid YAML file\n    - [ ] Test: validateYamlFile returns error for non-existent file\n    - [ ] Test: validateYamlFile returns error for invalid YAML file\n    - [ ] All tests pass with `bun test`\n\n### Script Registration\n\n- [ ] **T5**: Register validate script in package.json `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#8-deployment-design](design.md#8-deployment-design)\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] \"validate\" script added to package.json scripts section\n    - [ ] Script points to src/validate.ts\n    - [ ] `bun run validate <filepath>` invokes the validator correctly\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n- [ ] REQ-001: Command accepts single file path as command-line argument (`bun run validate <filepath>`)\n- [ ] REQ-002: Files with .yaml extension are processed\n- [ ] REQ-002: Files with .yml extension are processed\n- [ ] REQ-003: Valid YAML content passes validation\n- [ ] REQ-003: Invalid YAML content fails validation\n- [ ] REQ-004: Success message displayed for valid YAML files\n- [ ] REQ-005: Error message includes line number where syntax error was detected\n- [ ] REQ-005: Error message is human-readable\n- [ ] REQ-006: Exit code is 0 for valid YAML files\n- [ ] REQ-007: Exit code is non-zero for invalid YAML files\n- [ ] REQ-008: `bun run validate <filepath>` invokes the validation command\n- [ ] REQ-009: Appropriate error message displayed for non-existent files\n- [ ] REQ-009: Exit code is non-zero for non-existent files\n- [ ] REQ-010: Usage message displayed when no argument provided\n\n### User Stories\n\n- [ ] STORY-001: Running `bun run validate config.yaml` shows pass or fail message\n- [ ] STORY-002: Error message includes line reference for syntax errors\n- [ ] STORY-003: Exit code is 0 for valid files, non-zero for invalid files\n- [ ] STORY-004: Files with .yml extension validated same as .yaml files\n\n### Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- [ ] Validation time for files under 1MB is less than 1 second\n- [ ] Command reads files from local filesystem only (no remote URLs)\n- [ ] Command does not modify input files (read-only operation)\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] All unit tests passing\n- [ ] Documentation updated (package.json scripts and dependencies)\n"
