        "file_path": "/private/tmp/rp1-evals/e04cb325/workspace/.rp1/work/features/yaml-validator-command/design.md",
        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-01-30\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis design specifies a command-line YAML syntax validator for the rp1-eval-project. The validator reads a YAML file from the local filesystem, parses it using the js-yaml library, and reports success or failure with actionable error messages including line numbers.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph CLI[\"CLI Layer\"]\n        V[validate.ts]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Core[\"Core Layer\"]\n        YV[yaml-validator.ts]\n    end\n\n    subgraph External[\"External\"]\n        FS[Bun.file API]\n        JY[js-yaml]\n    end\n\n    V --> YV\n    YV --> FS\n    YV --> JY\n```\n\n**Data Flow**:\n1. User invokes `bun run validate <filepath>`\n2. `validate.ts` parses CLI arguments\n3. `yaml-validator.ts` reads file and validates YAML syntax\n4. Result (success/failure with details) returned to CLI\n5. CLI outputs message and sets exit code\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### Component Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph \"src/\"\n        validate[validate.ts<br/>CLI Entry Point]\n        validator[yaml-validator.ts<br/>Core Validation Logic]\n        validatorTest[yaml-validator.test.ts<br/>Unit Tests]\n    end\n\n    subgraph \"External Dependencies\"\n        jsyaml[js-yaml<br/>YAML Parser]\n        bunfile[Bun.file<br/>File System API]\n    end\n\n    validate -->|imports| validator\n    validator -->|imports| jsyaml\n    validator -->|uses| bunfile\n    validatorTest -->|tests| validator\n```\n\n### Component Responsibilities\n\n| Component | Responsibility |\n|-----------|---------------|\n| `validate.ts` | CLI argument parsing, output formatting, exit code management |\n| `yaml-validator.ts` | File reading, YAML parsing, error extraction, result formatting |\n| `js-yaml` | YAML syntax parsing with detailed error information |\n\n### Sequence Diagram: Validation Flow\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as validate.ts\n    participant Validator as yaml-validator.ts\n    participant FS as Bun.file\n    participant YAML as js-yaml\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate config.yaml\n    CLI->>CLI: Parse arguments\n\n    alt No argument provided\n        CLI->>User: Display usage, exit(1)\n    else Argument provided\n        CLI->>Validator: validateYamlFile(filepath)\n        Validator->>FS: Read file content\n\n        alt File not found\n            FS-->>Validator: Error\n            Validator-->>CLI: {success: false, error: \"File not found\"}\n            CLI->>User: Error message, exit(2)\n        else File exists\n            FS-->>Validator: File content\n            Validator->>YAML: yaml.load(content)\n\n            alt Valid YAML\n                YAML-->>Validator: Parsed object\n                Validator-->>CLI: {success: true, filepath}\n                CLI->>User: Success message, exit(0)\n            else Invalid YAML\n                YAML-->>Validator: YAMLException\n                Validator-->>CLI: {success: false, error, line}\n                CLI->>User: Error with line number, exit(1)\n            end\n        end\n    end\n```\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 Module: yaml-validator.ts\n\n**Purpose**: Core validation logic, isolated from CLI concerns for testability.\n\n**Interfaces**:\n\n```typescript\n/**\n * Result of YAML validation operation\n */\nexport interface ValidationResult {\n  /** Whether validation succeeded */\n  success: boolean;\n  /** File path that was validated */\n  filepath: string;\n  /** Error message if validation failed */\n  error?: string;\n  /** Line number where error occurred (1-indexed) */\n  line?: number;\n  /** Column number where error occurred (1-indexed) */\n  column?: number;\n}\n\n/**\n * Validates a YAML file for syntax correctness.\n *\n * @param filepath - Path to the YAML file to validate\n * @returns ValidationResult indicating success or failure with details\n */\nexport async function validateYamlFile(filepath: string): Promise<ValidationResult>;\n\n/**\n * Validates YAML content string for syntax correctness.\n * Useful for testing without file I/O.\n *\n * @param content - YAML content to validate\n * @param filepath - Optional filepath for error reporting\n * @returns ValidationResult indicating success or failure with details\n */\nexport function validateYamlContent(content: string, filepath?: string): ValidationResult;\n```\n\n**Implementation Notes**:\n- Uses `Bun.file(filepath).text()` for async file reading\n- Wraps `yaml.load()` in try-catch to capture YAMLException\n- Extracts line/column from `YAMLException.mark` property\n- Returns structured result for CLI to format\n\n### 3.2 Module: validate.ts\n\n**Purpose**: CLI entry point handling arguments, output, and exit codes.\n\n**Exit Codes**:\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| 0 | YAML file is valid |\n| 1 | YAML syntax error |\n| 2 | File not found or unreadable |\n\n**Output Format**:\n\n```\n# Success\nValid YAML: config.yaml\n\n# Syntax Error\nInvalid YAML: config.yaml\n  Error at line 15, column 3: unexpected end of the stream within a flow collection\n\n# File Not Found\nError: File not found: config.yaml\n\n# No Argument\nUsage: bun run validate <filepath>\n  Validates YAML syntax for .yaml or .yml files\n```\n\n### 3.3 Extension Validation\n\nThe validator accepts any file path but is designed for .yaml and .yml files. No extension enforcement is implemented (per requirements - files with these extensions \"are processed\" but no restriction on others).\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Rationale |\n|-------|------------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Project standard |\n| Language | TypeScript | Project standard |\n| YAML Parser | js-yaml | Well-established library with detailed error reporting |\n| File I/O | Bun.file API | Native Bun API, async-friendly |\n| Testing | bun:test | Project standard |\n\n### Dependency Addition\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"js-yaml\": \"^4.1.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| # | Component | Description | Files |\n|---|-----------|-------------|-------|\n| T1 | Dependency Setup | Add js-yaml to package.json | `package.json` |\n| T2 | Core Validator | Implement yaml-validator.ts with validation logic | `src/yaml-validator.ts` |\n| T3 | CLI Entry Point | Implement validate.ts with argument parsing and output | `src/validate.ts` |\n| T4 | Unit Tests | Test yaml-validator.ts functions | `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` |\n| T5 | Script Registration | Add \"validate\" script to package.json | `package.json` |\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation: add js-yaml dependency\n2. [T2] - Core module implementation (requires js-yaml)\n3. [T3, T4] - CLI and tests can be developed in parallel (both use validator)\n4. [T5] - Script registration (requires CLI to exist)\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (imports js-yaml library)\n- T3 -> T2 (imports validateYamlFile function)\n- T4 -> T2 (tests validateYamlContent function)\n- T5 -> T3 (script must point to existing entry point)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T3 -> T5\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Type | Value | Rationale |\n|-----------|-------|-----------|\n| Valid YAML parsing | HIGH | Core business logic |\n| Invalid YAML error extraction | HIGH | Core business logic with line numbers |\n| File not found handling | HIGH | App-specific error handling |\n| Empty file handling | MEDIUM | Edge case, YAML spec compliance |\n| CLI argument parsing | LOW | Simple pass-through, covered by integration |\n\n### Test Plan\n\n```typescript\n// src/yaml-validator.test.ts\n\ndescribe(\"yaml-validator\", () => {\n  describe(\"validateYamlContent\", () => {\n    test(\"returns success for valid YAML\");\n    test(\"returns success for empty content\");\n    test(\"returns error with line number for invalid YAML\");\n    test(\"returns error with column number for invalid YAML\");\n    test(\"handles YAML with comments\");\n    test(\"handles multi-document YAML\");\n  });\n\n  describe(\"validateYamlFile\", () => {\n    test(\"returns success for valid YAML file\");\n    test(\"returns error for non-existent file\");\n    test(\"returns error for invalid YAML file\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### Tests NOT Included (per test value assessment)\n\n- js-yaml library behavior verification (library responsibility)\n- Bun.file API behavior (runtime responsibility)\n- Exit code testing (integration/E2E scope)\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\n### Installation\n\n```bash\n# Install new dependency\nbun install\n```\n\n### Usage\n\n```bash\n# Validate a YAML file\nbun run validate path/to/config.yaml\n\n# Or directly\nbun run src/validate.ts path/to/config.yaml\n```\n\n### CI/CD Integration\n\n```yaml\n# Example GitHub Actions step\n- name: Validate config\n  run: bun run validate config.yaml\n```\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| edit | package.json | scripts | N/A | Add \"validate\" script |\n| edit | package.json | dependencies | N/A | Add js-yaml |\n\nNo README or documentation changes required per existing project conventions.\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML parsing library | js-yaml | User-approved, well-documented error reporting with line/column info | None (constraint relaxed) |\n| D2 | File structure | Separate validator module from CLI | Enables unit testing without CLI, follows separation of concerns | Single file (less testable) |\n| D3 | Exit code scheme | 0=success, 1=syntax error, 2=file error | Unix convention, distinguishes error types for CI/CD | Single non-zero code (less informative) |\n| D4 | Async file reading | Bun.file().text() | Native Bun API, consistent with modern async patterns | fs.readFileSync (blocking) |\n| D5 | Extension handling | No enforcement | Requirements specify support but not restriction | Reject non-.yaml/.yml (overly restrictive) |\n"
