        "old_string": "## Scripts\n\n- `bun run dev` - Run the main entry point\n- `bun test` - Run tests\n- `bun run lint` - Run linter\n- `bun run format` - Run formatter",
        "new_string": "## Scripts\n\n- `bun run dev` - Run the main entry point\n- `bun test` - Run tests\n- `bun run lint` - Run linter\n- `bun run format` - Run formatter\n- `bun run validate-yaml <filepath>` - Validate a YAML file for syntax errors\n\n## YAML Validator\n\nValidates YAML files for syntax correctness without external dependencies.\n\n### Usage\n\n```bash\nbun run validate-yaml path/to/file.yaml\n```\n\n### Output\n\n**Success:**\n```\nValid: path/to/file.yaml\n```\n\n**Syntax Error:**\n```\nInvalid: path/to/file.yaml\n  Line 5: Invalid indentation - expected 2 spaces, found 3\n```\n\n**File Not Found:**\n```\nError: File not found: path/to/file.yaml\n```\n\n### Exit Codes\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| 0 | Valid YAML - no syntax errors |\n| 1 | Invalid YAML or error (file not found, etc.) |\n\n### Limitations\n\n- Partial YAML specification coverage (common syntax patterns only)\n- Limited anchor (`&`) and alias (`*`) validation\n- No multi-document support (files with `---` separators)\n- Limited flow syntax validation (`{key: value}`, `[item]`)"
