ed validation, exit code is non-zero.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/0c034016/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:30-52\n- Evidence: Code `process.exit(1)` is called for all error conditions: FileNotFound (line 35), FileReadError (line 43), and validation errors (line 51). Verified with CLI tests: invalid YAML returned exit code 1, file not found returned exit code 1.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### REQ-004: Handle Missing or Inaccessible Files\n\n| Attribute | Value |\n|-----------|-------|\n| Priority | Must Have |\n| Requirement | The system shall display a clear error message when the specified file does not exist or cannot be read |\n\n**AC-004**: Given a non-existent file path, when the validator is run, then an appropriate error message is displayed and exit code is non-zero.\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation:\n  - `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/0c034016/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/yaml/validator.ts`:26-41 - File existence check\n  - `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/0c034016/workspace/.rp1/work/worktrees/feature-yaml-validator-command/src/validate-yaml.ts`:30-36 - CLI error display\n- Evidence: Validator checks `await file.exists()` and returns `FileNotFound` error type with message `File not found: <filepath>`. CLI displays \"Error: File not found: <filepath>\" and exits with code 1. Verified with: `bun run validate-yaml /nonexistent/file.yaml` displayed the error message and returned exit code 1.\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### REQ-005: No New Dependencies\n\n| Attribute | Value |\n|-----------|-------|\n| Priority | Must Have |\n| Requirement | The implementation shall not add any new external npm dependencies to package.json |\n\n**AC-005**: After implementation, package.json devDependencies and dependencies remain unchanged (except @types/bun if already present).\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/0c034