        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-01-30\n\n---\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis design specifies a command-line YAML syntax validator for the Bun TypeScript project. The validator will check YAML files for syntax correctness without adding external npm dependencies, using a custom-implemented syntax validation approach.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    CLI[CLI Entry Point<br/>validate-yaml.ts] --> Validator[YAML Validator<br/>validator.ts]\n    Validator --> FileReader[Bun File API]\n    Validator --> SyntaxChecker[Syntax Checker]\n    CLI --> Console[Console Output]\n    CLI --> ExitCode[Process Exit Code]\n```\n\n**Key Design Decisions:**\n- Custom YAML syntax validator (no external dependencies)\n- Separate CLI entry point following existing project patterns\n- Structured validation result for clear error reporting\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### 2.1 Component Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph CLI[\"CLI Layer\"]\n        Entry[validate-yaml.ts]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Core[\"Core Layer\"]\n        Validator[YAMLValidator]\n        SyntaxRules[Syntax Rules]\n    end\n\n    subgraph IO[\"I/O Layer\"]\n        FileIO[File Reader]\n        Output[Console Output]\n    end\n\n    Entry --> Validator\n    Validator --> SyntaxRules\n    Validator --> FileIO\n    Entry --> Output\n```\n\n### 2.2 Module Structure\n\n| Module | Location | Responsibility |\n|--------|----------|----------------|\n| CLI Entry | `src/validate-yaml.ts` | Command-line interface, argument parsing, output formatting |\n| Validator | `src/yaml/validator.ts` | Core validation logic, syntax checking |\n| Types | `src/yaml/types.ts` | TypeScript interfaces for validation results |\n\n### 2.3 Sequence Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as validate-yaml.ts\n    participant Validator as YAMLValidator\n    participant FS as File System\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate-yaml <filepath>\n    CLI->>CLI: Parse arguments\n    alt No filepath provided\n        CLI->>User: Error: No file path provided\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n    CLI->>Validator: validateFile(filepath)\n    Validator->>FS: Read file\n    alt File not found\n        FS-->>Validator: Error\n        Validator-->>CLI: ValidationResult(error)\n        CLI->>User: Error: File not found\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n    FS-->>Validator: File content\n    Validator->>Validator: Check empty content\n    alt Empty file\n        Validator-->>CLI: ValidationResult(invalid)\n        CLI->>User: Error: Empty file\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n    Validator->>Validator: Validate syntax\n    alt Syntax error\n        Validator-->>CLI: ValidationResult(invalid, errors)\n        CLI->>User: Error details with line number\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n    Validator-->>CLI: ValidationResult(valid)\n    CLI->>User: Success message\n    CLI->>CLI: exit(0)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 YAML Syntax Validator\n\nThe validator implements syntax checking for common YAML errors without using external parsing libraries. This approach checks for structural validity rather than full YAML specification compliance.\n\n**Validation Checks:**\n\n| Check | Description | Error Type |\n|-------|-------------|------------|\n| Empty content | File has no content or only whitespace | InvalidContent |\n| Indentation | Consistent spacing, no tabs for indentation | IndentationError |\n| Key-value syntax | Valid colon-separated key-value pairs | SyntaxError |\n| String quoting | Properly closed quotes | QuoteError |\n| List syntax | Valid list item markers | ListError |\n| Multiline strings | Proper multiline indicators | MultilineError |\n| Duplicate keys | Same key at same level | DuplicateKeyError |\n\n**Limitations (Documented):**\n- Does not validate against YAML schema\n- May not catch all edge cases of YAML 1.2 specification\n- Complex anchors and aliases have limited validation\n\n### 3.2 Type Definitions\n\n```typescript\n// src/yaml/types.ts\n\nexport interface ValidationError {\n  line: number;\n  column?: number;\n  message: string;\n  type: ErrorType;\n}\n\nexport type ErrorType =\n  | 'FileNotFound'\n  | 'FileReadError'\n  | 'EmptyFile'\n  | 'IndentationError'\n  | 'SyntaxError'\n  | 'QuoteError'\n  | 'ListError'\n  | 'DuplicateKeyError';\n\nexport interface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  filePath: string;\n  errors: ValidationError[];\n}\n```\n\n### 3.3 Validator Interface\n\n```typescript\n// src/yaml/validator.ts\n\n/**\n * Validate a YAML file for syntax correctness.\n * @param filePath - Path to the YAML file to validate\n * @returns ValidationResult with validation status and any errors\n */\nexport async function validateYamlFile(filePath: string): Promise<ValidationResult>;\n\n/**\n * Validate YAML content string for syntax correctness.\n * @param content - YAML content to validate\n * @param filePath - Optional file path for error reporting\n * @returns ValidationResult with validation status and any errors\n */\nexport function validateYamlContent(content: string, filePath?: string): ValidationResult;\n```\n\n### 3.4 CLI Interface\n\n```typescript\n// src/validate-yaml.ts\n\n/**\n * CLI entry point for YAML validation command.\n *\n * Usage: bun run validate-yaml <filepath>\n *\n * Exit codes:\n *   0 - Validation successful\n *   1 - Validation failed or error occurred\n */\n```\n\n**Command Usage:**\n```bash\nbun run validate-yaml path/to/file.yaml\n```\n\n**Output Format:**\n\nSuccess:\n```\nValid: path/to/file.yaml\n```\n\nFailure:\n```\nInvalid: path/to/file.yaml\n  Line 5: Invalid indentation - expected 2 spaces, found 3\n  Line 12: Unclosed quote starting at column 8\n```\n\nError (file not found):\n```\nError: File not found: path/to/file.yaml\n```\n\n### 3.5 Exit Codes\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| 0 | Validation successful - file is valid YAML |\n| 1 | Validation failed - syntax errors found |\n| 1 | Error - file not found or cannot be read |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Rationale |\n|-------|------------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript | Existing project language |\n| File I/O | Bun.file API | Built-in, no dependencies |\n| CLI Args | process.argv | Standard Node/Bun API |\n| Testing | bun:test | Existing test framework |\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- No new dependencies added\n- Uses only Bun built-in capabilities and standard JavaScript\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| # | Component | Description | Complexity |\n|---|-----------|-------------|------------|\n| T1 | YAML Validator Module | Core syntax validation logic with type definitions | Medium |\n| T2 | CLI Entry Point | Command-line interface with argument parsing and output | Low |\n| T3 | Unit Tests | Test coverage for validator and CLI | Medium |\n| T4 | Package.json Update | Add script entry for the command | Low |\n\n**Estimated Effort:** 4-6 hours\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation component with no dependencies\n2. [T2, T3] - Both depend on T1 being complete; CLI and tests can be developed in parallel\n3. [T4] - Final integration requiring CLI entry point\n\n**Dependencies:**\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports and uses validator functions)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: Tests import validator for testing)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: Script references entry point file)\n\n**Critical Path:** T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n---\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### 7.1 Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Category | Value | Rationale |\n|---------------|-------|-----------|\n| Syntax validation logic | HIGH | Core business logic - validates YAML correctly |\n| Error message formatting | MEDIUM | User-facing output quality |\n| File reading errors | HIGH | App-specific error handling |\n| Exit code behavior | HIGH | Contract for CI/CD integration |\n\n### 7.2 Test Cases\n\n**Unit Tests (src/yaml/validator.test.ts):**\n\n| Test | Description | Priority |\n|------|-------------|----------|\n| Valid YAML | Simple valid YAML returns valid result | Must Have |\n| Empty file | Empty content returns invalid with correct error | Must Have |\n| Indentation error | Inconsistent indentation detected | Must Have |\n| Unclosed quote | Missing closing quote detected | Must Have |\n| Invalid key-value | Malformed key:value syntax detected | Must Have |\n| File not found | Non-existent file returns appropriate error | Must Have |\n| Whitespace-only file | Treated as empty file | Should Have |\n| Complex valid YAML | Nested structures validate correctly | Should Have |\n\n**Integration Tests:**\n\n| Test | Description | Priority |\n|------|-------------|----------|\n| CLI success flow | Valid file returns exit code 0 | Must Have |\n| CLI failure flow | Invalid file returns exit code 1 | Must Have |\n| CLI error flow | Missing file returns exit code 1 | Must Have |\n| CLI no args | No file path shows usage error | Should Have |\n\n### 7.3 Test File Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  yaml/\n    validator.ts\n    validator.test.ts\n    types.ts\n  validate-yaml.ts\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\n### 8.1 Integration\n\nThe command integrates into the existing project via package.json scripts:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 8.2 Usage\n\n```bash\n# Validate a YAML file\nbun run validate-yaml config.yaml\n\n# Use in CI pipeline\nbun run validate-yaml config.yaml || exit 1\n```\n\n### 8.3 Rollout\n\nNo staged rollout required - feature is additive with no impact on existing functionality.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| add | README.md | Usage/Commands | N/A | Document new command availability |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML parsing approach | Custom syntax validator | No external dependencies allowed per REQ-005 | External library (rejected - adds dependency), Bun built-in (none exists) |\n| D2 | Module structure | Separate yaml/ directory | Clean separation, allows future expansion | Single file (rejected - poor organization) |\n| D3 | CLI entry point | Separate validate-yaml.ts | Follows existing pattern of index.ts, clean separation | Extend index.ts with subcommands (rejected - more complex) |\n| D4 | Error output format | Human-readable with line numbers | REQ-002 requires clear error messages | JSON output (could add as flag later) |\n| D5 | Exit code strategy | 0 for success, 1 for all failures | Simple, standard convention, meets REQ-003 | Different codes per error type (rejected - unnecessary complexity) |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: Known Limitations\n\nDue to the no-dependency constraint, the YAML validator has the following limitations:\n\n1. **Partial YAML Specification Coverage**: The validator checks common syntax patterns but does not implement the full YAML 1.2 specification.\n\n2. **Limited Anchor/Alias Validation**: YAML anchors (`&`) and aliases (`*`) have basic validation only.\n\n3. **No Multi-Document Support**: Files with multiple YAML documents (separated by `---`) are validated as a single document.\n\n4. **Complex Flow Syntax**: Inline flow syntax (`{key: value}`, `[item1, item2]`) has limited validation.\n\nThese limitations should be documented in user-facing documentation.\n"
