        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 5 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 days\n**Started**: 2026-01-30\n\n## Overview\n\nCommand-line YAML syntax validator for Bun TypeScript project. Uses custom-implemented syntax validation to check YAML files for common errors without adding external npm dependencies. The validator detects indentation errors, unclosed quotes, invalid key-value syntax, and other structural issues.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation component with no dependencies\n2. [T2, T3] - Both depend on T1 being complete; CLI and tests can be developed in parallel\n3. [T4] - Final integration requiring CLI entry point\n\n**Dependencies:**\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports and uses validator functions)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: Tests import validator for testing)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: Script references entry point file)\n\n**Critical Path:** T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Foundation\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement YAML Validator Module with type definitions `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-yaml-syntax-validator](design.md#31-yaml-syntax-validator)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Create `src/yaml/types.ts` with ValidationError, ErrorType, and ValidationResult interfaces\n    - [ ] Create `src/yaml/validator.ts` with validateYamlFile() and validateYamlContent() functions\n    - [ ] Implement empty content detection returning EmptyFile error\n    - [ ] Implement indentation validation (consistent spacing, no tabs)\n    - [ ] Implement key-value syntax validation (colon-separated pairs)\n    - [ ] Implement string quote validation (properly closed quotes)\n    - [ ] Implement list syntax validation (valid list item markers)\n    - [ ] Implement duplicate key detection at same level\n    - [ ] Return ValidationResult with line numbers for all detected errors\n    - [ ] Handle file not found and file read errors appropriately\n\n### CLI and Testing\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement CLI Entry Point with argument parsing and output formatting `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#34-cli-interface](design.md#34-cli-interface)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Create `src/validate-yaml.ts` as CLI entry point\n    - [ ] Parse file path from process.argv\n    - [ ] Display usage error when no file path provided\n    - [ ] Call validateYamlFile() and format output appropriately\n    - [ ] Display \"Valid: <filepath>\" for successful validation\n    - [ ] Display \"Invalid: <filepath>\" with error details (line number, message) for failures\n    - [ ] Display \"Error: File not found: <filepath>\" for missing files\n    - [ ] Return exit code 0 for valid YAML\n    - [ ] Return exit code 1 for invalid YAML or errors\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement unit and integration tests for validator and CLI `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#72-test-cases](design.md#72-test-cases)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Create `src/yaml/validator.test.ts` with unit tests\n    - [ ] Test valid YAML returns valid result (Must Have)\n    - [ ] Test empty file returns invalid with EmptyFile error (Must Have)\n    - [ ] Test inconsistent indentation is detected (Must Have)\n    - [ ] Test unclosed quote is detected (Must Have)\n    - [ ] Test malformed key:value syntax is detected (Must Have)\n    - [ ] Test non-existent file returns FileNotFound error (Must Have)\n    - [ ] Test whitespace-only file treated as empty (Should Have)\n    - [ ] Test complex nested structures validate correctly (Should Have)\n    - [ ] Test CLI success flow returns exit code 0 (Must Have)\n    - [ ] Test CLI failure flow returns exit code 1 (Must Have)\n    - [ ] Test CLI with missing file returns exit code 1 (Must Have)\n\n### Integration\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Update package.json with validate-yaml script entry `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#81-integration](design.md#81-integration)\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Add \"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\" to package.json scripts\n    - [ ] Verify command runs successfully with `bun run validate-yaml <filepath>`\n    - [ ] Confirm no new dependencies added to package.json\n\n### User Docs\n\n- [ ] **TD1**: Create documentation for README.md - Usage/Commands `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#documentation-impact](design.md#documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: add\n\n    **Target**: README.md\n\n    **Section**: Usage/Commands\n\n    **KB Source**: -\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] New section created documenting validate-yaml command\n    - [ ] Usage example included: `bun run validate-yaml <filepath>`\n    - [ ] Output format documented (success/failure messages)\n    - [ ] Exit codes documented (0 = valid, 1 = invalid/error)\n    - [ ] Known limitations noted (partial YAML spec coverage)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\nFrom requirements.md:\n\n- [ ] REQ-001: Given a valid YAML file, validator reports success; given invalid YAML, reports syntax error\n- [ ] REQ-002: Error messages include line number (if available) and error description\n- [ ] REQ-003: Exit code 0 on successful validation, non-zero on failure\n- [ ] REQ-004: Clear error message when file does not exist or cannot be read\n- [ ] REQ-005: No new entries in package.json dependencies or devDependencies\n- [ ] REQ-006: Success confirmation message displayed for valid YAML\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All tasks completed\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] Tests passing with adequate coverage\n- [ ] Documentation updated (README.md)\n- [ ] No new npm dependencies added\n"
